// The invariants of `gopp fmt` on the Go++ sources of the repository:
//   parse(print(parse(src))) == parse(src)  (imports unsorted; empty statements,
//                                           redundant parentheses and number
//                                           spelling excepted, as in gofmt)
//   fmt(fmt(src)) == fmt(src)
//   no comment is lost.
// Files with syntax errors (the diagnostics tests) are skipped.

// The ten spec examples.
// RUN: %python %S/check-corpus.py %gopp %examples --min 10

// Every test input that is a valid program: parse and lex tests (the sema
// tests are in roundtrip-sema.test, so each test stays under the 2 s limit).
// RUN: %python %S/check-corpus.py %gopp --ext .test --min 15 %S/../parse %S/../lex

// The formatter's own goldens.
// RUN: %python %S/check-corpus.py %gopp --ext .golden --min 10 %S/Inputs
